        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofdallas.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area was primarily inhabited by Chippewa Indians until white hunters and trappers began visiting around 1868.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dallas_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office originally named Sylvan Springs was established in 1877 before being renamed Dallas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dallas_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The arrival of the Rice Lake, Dallas and Menomonie Railroad in 1900 led to the village's formal incorporation in 1903.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dallas_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dallas celebrates an annual Oktoberfest festival on the first Saturday in October every year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
